23:T3351,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"SoftwareApplication","@id":"https://keplar.one/#app","name":"Keplar","applicationCategory":"BusinessApplication","applicationSubCategory":"Multi-model AI assistant and AI workspace","operatingSystem":"Web, Windows, macOS, Linux","url":"https://keplar.one/","description":"Keplar One (keplar.one) is an AI workspace for everyday questions, studying, research and making things. Its engine, Keplar-One, sends a question to the AI models it needs, compares their answers claim by claim, investigates where they disagree and writes one answer with the agreement and disagreements shown. Around that engine, Keplar is a full set of tools: Reason, Deep Research and Debate modes; Study mode with flashcards, quizzes and study plans; a slideshow maker; image and video generation; Create, which builds and publishes real websites and apps; Roblox Studio and Blender co-builders in the desktop app; projects, memory, specialists and connected apps; and a public API and embeddable widget. Keplar Business (business.keplar.one) is a separate desktop app for companies, with scheduled agents, approvals, team workspaces and a business dashboard.","publisher":{"@id":"https://keplar.one/#organization"},"creator":[{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://keplar.one/about#hassen-keder","name":"Hassen Keder","givenName":"Hassen","familyName":"Keder","jobTitle":"Co-founder","worksFor":{"@id":"https://keplar.one/#organization"}},{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://keplar.one/about#hussain-keder","name":"Hussain Keder","givenName":"Hussain","familyName":"Keder","jobTitle":"Co-founder","worksFor":{"@id":"https://keplar.one/#organization"}}],"author":[{"@id":"https://keplar.one/about#hassen-keder"},{"@id":"https://keplar.one/about#hussain-keder"}],"featureList":["Model routing: Classifies each question by kind and difficulty, then asks only the models it needs, weighed by quality, reliability, latency and cost. Free uses free open models; paid plans add premium models from several providers.","Claim-by-claim comparison: The models answer independently and in parallel, so no answer anchors the others. Keplar breaks the answers into claims and compares them.","Disagreement map: Shows where the models agree, where they split and why the answer went the way it did. A disagreement is flagged, never silently resolved.","Evaluation, not voting: A majority is not treated as the truth. Keplar weighs the evidence and reasoning behind each answer, so one dissenting model with the better argument can win.","Answer breakdown: Under every answer: Consensus (agreement percentage and how many models agreed), Models consulted, Sources the models cite, Disagreements, Verification and a Reasoning summary.","Reason mode: Works the problem through step by step and shows how the answer was checked. Paid plans add a model to the panel.","Deep Research: Longer, multi-step research into a report for big decisions. Uses more of your monthly usage.","Debate mode: The models argue in rounds and read each other's points before Keplar writes one answer. Uses more usage.","Voice and Talk: Ask out loud and hear the answer read back; press and hold to talk. Keplar does not record or store your audio.","Live demo: Ask a real question on the home page without an account.","Shared answers: Publish an answer you are proud of to a public page that shows the question, how many models agreed and where they differed.","Web lookups: Live web search inside answers. Shown in the app but not switched on yet.","Images and screenshots: Charts, receipts, whiteboards and interfaces, sent only to models that can see.","Video: Keyframes are sampled in your browser, so the clip itself is never uploaded.","Documents, code and data: PDF, text, CSV, JSON and source files, read as text; coding help and file analysis on paid plans.","Word, PowerPoint, Excel and audio: Office files parsed safely and audio transcribed.","Links: Paste a URL and Keplar reads the page through a guarded fetch.","Study mode: Upload a text-based PDF or paste notes and get an outline, a plain-English summary, flashcards with spaced review, quizzes and a day-by-day plan to your exam date. Questions are answered only from your material, with page references, and Keplar says when something is not in it.","Slideshow maker: Turns a topic, outline or notes into a deck with titles, bullet points, speaker notes and an image idea per slide. Edit it, present it full screen, export to PowerPoint or PDF.","Guides, docs and a glossary: Plain-English guides on checking AI answers, product docs, a prompt library and an AI glossary.","Websites and web apps: Builds full sites and apps from a brief, with a code editor, terminal and live preview side by side. A written design rubric and a lint pass reject the generic AI look (purple glows, gradient blobs, three-card grids) before you see it.","Voice Live Create: Speak and watch the editor, terminal and preview build at the same time; say \"actually\" to change course. Needs a browser with speech recognition.","Surprise me: One press picks a specific brief, style and depth and builds it.","Version history and rollback: Every build is a version. Restore any one, branch it into a new draft, or roll back a change that went wrong.","Watch the code being written: While Create builds an app, the files appear as they are written, with a Tasks checklist of the plan and Ctrl+P to jump to any file.","Templates and community gallery: Start from a real site and describe what to change. Sites people chose to share can be liked, remixed and reported.","Showcase: Demo sites and apps by the Keplar team that set the bar Create is held to.","Image generation: Make pictures from a message or in the Images studio; attach an image to use as a reference.","Video generation: Generate short videos in Create's Video tab.","Mobile apps: Build mobile app projects in Create's Mobile tab.","Product import: Paste a product page link and Keplar's fetcher (KeplarBot, which obeys robots.txt) brings in the product details for a page about it.","Builds inside Studio: Looks at your place first (a screenshot and the Explorer tree), writes a numbered plan, then builds it step by step: maps, buildings, lighting, UI, effects and working Luau scripts, organized in named folders.","You play-test it: Keplar reads the output log for script errors and fixes them, then ends with a short \"How to test it\" list. A Play test button starts and stops play mode in Studio directly, so testing costs no AI usage; you say what to change.","A saved chat per game: Each game's conversation, plan and progress are saved on the device and synced to your Keplar account, so you can close Studio and Keplar and pick up where you left off, even on another computer.","Matches references: Attach screenshots or a clip of a UI, effect or game to match. For effects and UI it reuses Zonito's free particle pack, or makes its own textures in Studio.","Effects that look right: Flipbook particles from valid 1024 by 1024 sheets in the grid their creator states, self-lit glows with bright cores, scene-lit smoke behind them, and layered effects kept light on performance.","You stay in control: Reads run on their own; changes wait for approval unless you turn on auto-approve for safe changes; deleting, publishing, data stores and uploading images to your Roblox account always ask first.","Roblox Cloud overnight jobs: Give it a goal, a credit budget and a time limit, then close your computer: it works on your game's scripts on Keplar's servers, checks every edit with Luau's own analyzer, and leaves changes you review and apply in Studio. Scripts only; it can't play-test.","Always Claude Opus 5.5: Studio mode and Roblox Cloud run on Claude Opus 5.5 only. If it can't be used, the build pauses instead of switching to another model.","Floating overlay: A movable, always-on-top panel keeps the build chat next to Studio or Blender, with a switch between the two.","Models from a description: Reads the scene as compact text, plans, then builds with clean topology and modifiers at real-world scale, every object named and grouped in a collection.","Real PBR textures: Searches Poly Haven (free, CC0) and applies a full material set: color, roughness, normal, ambient occlusion and displacement, unwrapping meshes that have no UVs.","Procedural materials, lighting and props: Node-based materials for stylized looks, HDRI lighting and Poly Haven model import.","Export for games: Exports to FBX (imports into Roblox Studio), GLB or OBJ in Documents/Keplar exports.","Safe by default: The add-on only listens on this computer behind a secret key. Keplar's Python may not touch files, the network or other apps, or save or close Blender; deleting always asks, and every change waits for approval unless you turn on auto-approve.","Cheap to run: A short cached prompt, text scene summaries instead of screenshots, and small thinking budgets keep each step's AI usage low. Each .blend file's chat is saved and synced to your account.","Blender Cloud rendering: Renders the open scene on Keplar's servers with Blender 5.2 (Cycles, EEVEE or Workbench, on CPUs), so you can close Blender or turn your computer off; the scene is packed with its textures, the machine has no internet access, and the frames and an optional MP4 download to Documents/Keplar renders. Charged by machine time, with a budget and a time limit; renders are kept three days.","Real-time collaboration: Invite by link and edit the same project together with live cursors, follow mode and a shared terminal and preview.","AI critic: Rules, accessibility checks in a real browser and a separate model review your build, then apply the fixes you pick.","One-click publish and previews: Every draft gets a private preview link; publish it to a live keplar.site address in one step.","Custom domains with HTTPS: Connect a domain you own; Keplar checks the DNS, tells you what to change and issues certificates.","Deployments: Every published site and app in one list, with its versions.","Projects: Keep related chats, files and work together in a project.","Chat history and memory: Chats are saved to your account to reopen, rename and delete. With memory on, Keplar remembers durable things you tell it (name, goals, preferences) and keeps short summaries of recent chats. Memory is optional and under your control.","Specialists: Custom specialists people make and share. Add one to your account and Keplar's panel of models answers with it; shared ones are reviewed before listing.","Connected apps (MCP): Connect remote MCP servers such as Context7, DeepWiki, Microsoft Learn and Cloudflare Docs (Linear, Notion and Sentry sign-in in beta). Their tools start off and need approval.","Keplar Canvas: When you come back signed in, the Canvas home picks up where you left off.","Desktop app: For Windows, macOS and Linux. Keeps the app in its own window and adds the Roblox Studio and Blender co-builders; your account and data stay in the cloud.","Browser extension: Keplar One for Chrome and Edge: ask about a selection or a page from the toolbar or right-click menu, or use Search with Keplar One to drag over any text or picture on a page and get the answer in a side panel. Uses a Keplar API key; submitted to the Chrome Web Store.","Public API: Ask Keplar from your own code with Bearer keys, streaming, an OpenAPI spec and per-plan limits. Free keys use free models only.","Embeddable widget: One script tag puts Keplar Ask on your site, limited to the origins you allow.","Referral program: Invite a friend and you both get extra usage, never cash.","Languages: The website is published in 25 languages, and you can ask questions in your own language.","No overclaiming: Keplar is a practical multi-model workspace. It is not AGI or superintelligence, and agreement between models does not prove an answer is correct. Health, legal and money answers are general information, not professional advice.","Privacy and security: Files you attach are read for that question and not kept; voice is not recorded; a security page explains encryption, providers, retention and how to report a problem.","Changelog, roadmap and status: Dated release notes, a public roadmap of what is in beta or coming soon, and a live status page."],"offers":[{"@type":"Offer","name":"Free","price":"0","priceCurrency":"USD","url":"https://keplar.one/pricing"},{"@type":"Offer","name":"Keplar Lite","price":"20","priceCurrency":"USD","url":"https://keplar.one/pricing","priceSpecification":{"@type":"UnitPriceSpecification","price":"20","priceCurrency":"USD","billingDuration":"P1M","unitCode":"MON"}},{"@type":"Offer","name":"Keplar Plus","price":"45","priceCurrency":"USD","url":"https://keplar.one/pricing","priceSpecification":{"@type":"UnitPriceSpecification","price":"45","priceCurrency":"USD","billingDuration":"P1M","unitCode":"MON"}},{"@type":"Offer","name":"Keplar Pro","price":"99","priceCurrency":"USD","url":"https://keplar.one/pricing","priceSpecification":{"@type":"UnitPriceSpecification","price":"99","priceCurrency":"USD","billingDuration":"P1M","unitCode":"MON"}}]}d:["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$23"}}]
